FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] tooling/vscode/syntaxes/redblue.tmLanguage.json:7 — shipped grammar (generated by src/lsp.rs:219, configured by tooling/vscode/language-configuration.json:3) defines comments as `#.*$` with `lineComment: "#"`, but the language only accepts `//` comments (docs/GRAMMAR.md:25, SPEC.md:116, src/lexer.rs:366) and the lexer rejects `#` via src/lexer.rs:453-460 — an editor will dim `#` lines as comments and `Ctrl+/` will insert `#`, yet `rb diagnostics`/`rb run` fails on them, while real `//` comments get no highlighting — change the generator, shipped JSON, and language-configuration to `//` and add a test pinning it.
2. [MAJOR] src/linter.rs:44 — unused-variable warnings are emitted by iterating `defined_vars: HashSet<String>` (src/linter.rs:8), whose order is per-process random, and src/lsp.rs:134-142 plus src/lsp.rs:166-170 forward that order unchanged into the diagnostics JSON array — a file with two unused variables yields nondeterministic output ordering — sort the findings (or use a BTreeSet/sorted vec) and add a multi-warning ordering test.
3. [MINOR] src/lsp.rs:100-124 — `diagnostics()` tokenizes and parses the source, then calls `linter::lint(source)` which re-tokenizes and re-parses the same source (src/linter.rs:271-281), so the frontend runs twice per invocation despite the "runs once" claim — thread the tokens/AST through or correct the claim.
4. [MINOR] src/lsp.rs:79 — `Diagnostic::to_json` is documented as "The LSP `Diagnostic` shape" (see also src/lsp.rs:26-27, src/lsp.rs:35-41), but `{line,column,severity:"error"|"warning",message}` with 1-based positions is not LSP (which uses `range:{start:{line,character},end}`, numeric severity, 0-based lines) — reword as editor-specific JSON or emit real LSP.
5. [STYLE] src/lsp.rs:215-223 — the comment states strings come before comments, but the code pushes the comment pattern (src/lsp.rs:219) before the string pattern (src/lsp.rs:220-223), describing the opposite of what is built — fix the comment (and confirm the intended TextMate precedence).
